---
// Comparison page. Copy authored against briefs/maltipoo-vs-bichon-frise.json (2026-07-13).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PawTrail from '../components/PawTrail.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import CaptionedBlock from '../components/CaptionedBlock.astro';
import FactsCard from '../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site, whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../assets/site/50-maltipoo-vs-bichon-frise.webp';

const title = 'Maltipoo vs Bichon Frise: Puff or Velcro | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Maltipoo vs Bichon Frise for Singapore homes: sturdier merry powder-puff vs featherweight velcro lap dog. Coat workload, size and HDB status compared.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Compare Breeds', url: '/compare-maltipoo' },
  { name: 'Maltipoo vs Bichon Frise', url: '/maltipoo-vs-bichon-frise' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Which sheds less, a Maltipoo or a Bichon Frise?',
    a: 'Both are famously low-shedding. The difference is upkeep: the Bichon’s dense double coat needs serious daily brushing to stay that way, while the Maltipoo’s single-cross coat asks for a few sessions a week.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Bichon grooming more expensive?',
    a: 'Often one tier up, because salons price by weight and coat density and the Bichon carries more of both. Budget the fuller end of the $80 to $130 full-groom range and more frequent visits to keep the powder-puff shape.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which is better with young children?',
    a: 'The Bichon, structurally: at 5 to 8kg it is sturdier under enthusiastic hugs. A 2 to 4kg Maltipoo does fine with supervised, gentle kids, but it is the more fragile of the two.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which barks more?',
    a: 'The Maltipoo, slightly; its Maltese alert streak runs louder than the Bichon’s merry sociability. Both settle with early quiet training and enough company.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are both HDB approved?',
    a: 'Yes. The Bichon Frise is named at item 4 of HDB’s approved list, and the Maltipoo qualifies through item 62 as a cross of two approved breeds.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/maltipoo-vs-bichon-frise',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltipoo vs Bichon Frise comparison',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/maltipoo-vs-bichon-frise" schemas={schemas}>
  <section class="container-site pt-4">
    <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12 relative overflow-hidden rise-in">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="absolute -top-8 -right-8 w-44 h-44 text-white/40" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute top-6 right-[22%] w-9 h-9 text-primary/25 float-soft" style="--float-rot: 14deg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute bottom-5 right-[10%] w-7 h-7 text-primary/20 float-soft" style="--float-rot: -10deg; animation-delay: -2.6s" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute -bottom-10 -left-10 w-40 h-40 text-primary/8" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <div class="absolute bottom-2 left-0 right-0 opacity-30"><PawTrail /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="relative">
      <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Comparison</p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[24ch]">Maltipoo vs Bichon Frise</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[52ch] mb-5">
        The merry powder puff against the featherweight shadow. Similar looks from across the
        void deck, very different daily lives.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappLink('Hi! Could you help me decide between a Maltipoo and a Bichon Frise?')} class="btn-cta">Ask which fits you</a>
    </div></div>
  </section>

  <AnswerCapsule question="Maltipoo or Bichon Frise: what is the difference?">
    The difference between Maltipoo and Bichon Frise is size and coat workload. A Bichon Frise is the sturdier, merrier extrovert: 5 to 8kg, a white powder-puff double
    coat, and sociable with everyone it meets. A Maltipoo is the featherweight velcro dog: 2
    to 4kg, an apricot low-shedding coat, bonded hardest to its own people. Both are
    HDB-listed; coat workload and size are the practical deciders.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <section class="container-site pt-8">
    <img
      src={featuredImg.src}
      width={featuredImg.width}
      height={featuredImg.height}
      alt="Apricot Maltipoo beside a white powder-puff Bichon Frise on a light sofa"
      loading="lazy"
      class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]"
    />
  </section>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Size and sturdiness" id="size">
    <p>
      The bichon frise vs maltipoo size gap changes household maths. At 5 to 8kg the Bichon
      is robust enough for a home full of visiting grandchildren; at 2 to 4kg the toy
      Maltipoo needs the hugging supervised, as the <a href="/maltipoo-size">size guide</a>
      spells out, and in exchange rides carriers, laps and MRT journeys effortlessly.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Size maths"
      items={[
        'Bichon: 5 to 8kg, sturdier with kids',
        'Maltipoo: 2 to 4kg, featherweight and portable',
        'Both: flat-sized, short-walk breeds',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The coat workload gap" id="coat" reverse>
    <p>
      Both coats read "fluffy white-ish cloud" from a distance; up close the workload
      differs. The Bichon's dense double coat is what makes the powder-puff silhouette, and
      it demands genuine daily brushing plus frequent professional shaping. The Maltipoo's
      single-cross coat wants a few brushes a week and the standard four-to-six-week groom.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tear stains visit both; the whiter the face, the louder they read. The
      <a href="/blog/maltipoo-tear-stains">daily wipe routine</a> is the answer in either
      case.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Coat, honestly"
      items={[
        'Bichon: double coat, daily brushing, frequent shaping',
        'Maltipoo: lighter routine, few brushes a week',
        'Both: low-shedding, tear-stain prone',
        'Grooming budget: Bichon usually a tier up',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Temperament: merry vs devoted" id="temperament" tinted>
    <p>
      A Bichon loves the whole world: guests, neighbours, the delivery rider. A Maltipoo
      loves the world politely and its own people ferociously, per the
      <a href="/maltipoo-temperament">temperament guide</a>. Both want company; the Bichon
      copes a little better when the flat empties, the Maltipoo repays presence more
      intensely.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Character split"
      items={[
        'Bichon: sociable extrovert, crowd-pleaser',
        'Maltipoo: devoted velcro, favourite-person dog',
        'Alone tolerance: Bichon slightly higher',
        'Both: happiest in homes with company',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Who should pick which" id="verdict">
    <p>
      Pick the Bichon for a busy, social, kid-filled household that can fund and enjoy the
      coat ritual. Pick the Maltipoo for a quieter home that wants one small shadow on the
      sofa and a lighter grooming load. On paperwork they tie: Bichon at item 4 of the
      <a href="https://www.hdb.gov.sg/managing-my-home/home-ownership/keeping-pets" rel="noopener" target="_blank">HDB approved list</a>,
      Maltipoo via item 62.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The one-line verdict"
      items={[
        'Social household, kids, coat budget: Bichon',
        'Lap-first home, lighter coat work: Maltipoo',
        'HDB: both approved, no tiebreaker there',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Living with each, hour by hour" id="daily-life">
    <p>
      The daily rhythms diverge more than the photos suggest. A Bichon greets the household, does its rounds, and settles near the action; a Maltipoo appoints one person and supervises them full-time. In a busy family flat the Bichon's crowd-pleasing is a feature; in a quieter home the Maltipoo's shadowing is the whole point.
    </p>
    <p>
      On shedding, both sit at the low end, which is why both appear on every allergy shortlist. The honest nuance: no dog is allergen-free, dander and saliva travel with every coat type, and the only test that counts is time spent with the actual breed before you commit. We tell every sniffly buyer the same thing, and our <a href="/blog/maltipoo-hypoallergenic-shedding">shedding guide</a> puts it in writing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Exercise needs are close: two short walks and indoor play cover either, timed around the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-hot-weather">heat clock</a>. The gap is guests and noise: a Bichon works the room; a Maltipoo announces the room, then retires to a lap, which the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-barking">barking guide</a> explains how to manage.
    </p>
    <p>
      Budget-wise the two cost similar to feed and licence, but the Bichon's denser coat books more salon hours over a year. Either way the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-cost-ownership">ownership ledger</a> is the same maths with different grooming lines.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Hour-by-hour split"
      items={[
        "Bichon: greets everyone, settles anywhere",
        "Maltipoo: appoints one person, supervises",
        "Both low-shed; neither allergen-free",
        "Same walk needs, same heat clock",
        "Bichon books more salon hours yearly"
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />

  <CtaClose
    secondaryHeading="Compare more breeds"
    secondaryText="Cavapoo, Maltese, Toy Poodle, Shih Tzu and Cockapoo, all against the Maltipoo."
    secondaryHref="/compare-maltipoo"
    secondaryLabel="See all comparisons"
  />
</BaseLayout>
